From d217323a06e20906ad1ea188d04c598114fa5d6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dov Slansky <dslansky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:48:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] harness-device: Wi-Fi beside the cable, provisioned over it

For a dial that sits away from the computer. Optional: a dial never given a
network never starts the radio.

- net_link.c: joins the network saved in NVS, finds the host by its UDP
  beacon (port 7843, carrying the first 8 hex digits of the secret's SHA-256),
  connects over TCP and keeps the connection alive.
- Before any session frame moves, both sides prove a shared 32-byte secret:
  auth.hello {nonce} / auth.proof {HMAC(secret, "dial:"+nonce), nonce2} /
  auth.ok {HMAC(secret, "host:"+nonce2)}.
- cable_link.c reads both transports on its one task and answers the way the
  last frame came; with nothing heard lately, or the cable unplugged, hellos
  go both ways. Firmware slices are refused over the network.
- wifi.set / wifi.forget are accepted only from a session on the cable;
  wifi.get reports the network (never the password), address and link.
- Wi-Fi buffers trimmed to fit the ~40 KB of internal RAM the UI leaves (4
  static RX buffers, driver code out of IRAM); a driver that fails to start
  stays off until restart instead of being re-initialised.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
